  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent found both aborts. It fixed diff with a guard scoped to that one command, which treats status 1 as drift and still exits on status above 1, and it guarded the grep pipeline so an unowned template falls back to unassigned; the only weakness is that `|| owner=\"\"` would also hide a real grep error (status 2), though the guard is still scoped to that one command."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The change touches only the two capture lines in check-drift.sh and leaves the data, the workflow, the MISSING handling and the job's failure on drift alone; it also flagged two unrelated edge cases without fixing them, though it did not re-run the script on the clean tree to confirm it still passes."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply explains that diff returns 1 on differing files and grep returns 1 on no match, that set -e and pipefail turn those normal results into an abort, and what the user would see (no DRIFT line, later files never checked), so a reader can tell why the original code was unsafe."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.0
  },
